[
  {
    "kind": "plain_reply",
    "runId": "run_qa078_export_2",
    "role": "contributor1",
    "outcome": "completed",
    "text": "I read both assigned sources in full with `evidence.read_evidence`: `evidence_qa078_api_storage` and `evidence_qa078_security`.\n\n**Findings**\n\n`createExport` violates the idempotency contract for same-tenant replay with changed payload. The contract says the same `requestKey` with different normalized `format/filter` must conflict without new or changed data, but `createExport` returns any existing row matching `(tenantId, requestKey)` without comparing `payloadHash` (`evidence_qa078_api_storage`, `apiContract.idempotency`, `createExport`). Concrete input: tenant `t1`, request key `k`, first body `{format:\"csv\", filter:\"status=open\", requestKey:\"k\"}`, second body `{format:\"csv\", filter:\"status=closed\", requestKey:\"k\"}`. Observed consequence: second caller receives the first job as if its changed request were accepted/replayed. Safe repair: after loading `existing`, compare `existing.payloadHash` to the newly computed hash; return existing only on match, otherwise throw a conflict error and do not mutate jobs/outbox.\n\n`download` does not enforce current membership for the signed user. The security contract requires every download to check current active membership for `tenantId/userId` in the link and deny an unexpired link after revocation (`evidence_qa078_security`, `securityContract.download`). `issueLink` checks membership at issuance, but `download` only validates signature/expiry, loads a ready job by `jobId/tenantId`, and returns `store.get(job.objectKey)`. Concrete consequence: a user can receive a valid link, have membership revoked, and still download until `expiresAt`. Safe repair: after `decode`, check `members.has(`${value.tenantId}/${value.userId}`)` before reading the object, and keep the existing signature, expiry, tenant, and ready-state checks.\n\nThe database-side worker publication fence is good, but object-store writes are not fenced in the evidence shown. `finish` only publishes ready state when `id`, `tenantId`, `state='running'`, `epoch`, and `leaseUntil > now` match (`evidence_qa078_api_storage`, `claim`, `finish`). That preserves stale-worker DB protection. However, `finish(db, job, objectKey, now)` receives an already chosen object key, and no source shows store write ordering, conditional put, temporary keys, or cleanup fencing. Concrete race: worker A claims epoch 1, lease expires, worker B claims epoch 2 and writes/publishes object `final-key`; worker A later writes to the same `final-key` or cleanup deletes it after its `finish` fails. The DB will reject A’s stale `finish`, but the object store can still be overwritten or removed unless keys and cleanup are epoch-scoped. Safe repair: write to per-job/per-epoch temporary keys, publish only the winning key through `finish`, and allow cleanup only for non-published keys or keys whose epoch is not current.\n\n**Confirmed Correct Behavior To Preserve**\n\nCreation uses `requireSession(ctx)` and stores `ctx.tenantId/ctx.userId`; the body tenant is ignored by implementation shape (`evidence_qa078_api_storage`, `requireSession`, `createExport`). Job lookup for user routes is tenant-scoped through `getOwned`.\n\nTenant-local uniqueness exists via `UNIQUE(tenantId, requestKey)`, so different tenants may reuse the same request key while one tenant cannot create two rows for it.\n\nAccepted job creation and outbox insertion are in one SQLite transaction, with `afterInsert()` modeling rollback before the outbox insert (`createExport`). Preserve this atomic job/outbox behavior.\n\n`claim` and `finish` implement useful DB fencing: ready/canceled jobs are not claimable, expired running claims are reclaimable, and `finish` requires matching epoch, tenant, running state, and unexpired lease. `cancelExport` increments epoch, which invalidates unfinished workers at DB publication time.\n\nReady and canceled duplicates are no-ops for worker claiming because `claim` returns `null` unless state is `queued` or `running`.\n\n**Recovery Assessment**\n\nThe assigned sources contain the outbox table and atomic insertion, but no dispatcher, broker publish, acknowledgement, restart scan, or delivery deduplication implementation. I cannot confirm behavior for dispatcher crash, pre-delivery broker failure, lost acknowledgement after delivery, restart, or duplicate delivery from these sources.\n\nA safe design consistent with the evidence would be: commit job and unsent outbox together; dispatcher reads unsent outbox rows; publish to broker before marking `sentAt`; if publish fails before delivery, leave `sentAt NULL` for retry; if acknowledgement is lost after delivery, retry may publish the same event again, so consumers/workers must deduplicate or rely on idempotent `claim`/`finish` fences. This should be described as at-least-once delivery; exactly-once external execution is not supported by the available evidence.\n\n**Regression Plan**\n\nTest same key with changed payload: create tenant `t1` job with request key `k` and filter `a`; replay with same key and filter `b`; expect conflict, original job unchanged, no second job, no second outbox row.\n\nTest tenant/body boundaries: create with verified ctx tenant `t1` while body claims tenant `t2`; expect stored tenant `t1`. Reuse same request key under verified tenant `t2`; expect separate job allowed.\n\nTest transaction rollback: inject `afterInsert` throwing inside `createExport`; expect neither job nor outbox row persists. Then retry without injection; expect both job and outbox row persist.\n\nTest recovery delivery modes once dispatcher evidence exists: simulate publish failure before delivery and verify `sentAt` remains unset and restart republishes; simulate lost acknowledgement after delivery and verify duplicate broker delivery does not create duplicate execution beyond idempotent claim/finish behavior.\n\nTest old/new worker object race: worker A claims epoch 1 and writes/pauses; lease expires; worker B claims epoch 2, writes, and publishes ready; A resumes and attempts write/finish/cleanup. Expect DB remains on B’s object and A cannot overwrite or delete the published object.\n\nTest cancellation during paused work: worker claims, cancellation increments epoch, worker resumes and calls `finish`; expect `finish` false, job remains canceled, and any temporary object is cleaned without touching published/canceled state.\n\nTest revoked membership download: issue ready-job link for active member, revoke `${tenantId}/${userId}`, download before expiry; expect membership error and no `store.get`.\n\nTest normal downloads: ready job link downloads object before expiry; expired token is rejected; duplicate worker delivery for already ready job cannot reclaim or republish.\n\n**Unresolved Evidence Needs**\n\nReal remote-store/IAM/consistency/durability configuration is not included. Resolving this needs deployment/object-store configuration, IAM policy, bucket/key policy, conditional write support, lifecycle/cleanup rules, and consistency guarantees.\n\nProduction load, lease latency, and recovery-time measurements are not included. Resolving this needs measured worker runtimes, clock skew assumptions, queue/broker retry timing, dispatcher restart behavior, lease-expiry distribution, and duplicate-delivery rates under load.\n\nThe scripted/local source checks above are review-derived expectations, not production verification and not executed regression results.\n\n**Release Recommendation**\n\nI would not recommend release based on the confirmed idempotency and revoked-link authorization blockers, plus the object-store fencing and recovery evidence gaps. Repair order: fix idempotency conflict handling; add membership enforcement to `download`; define and test outbox dispatcher retry/duplicate semantics; fence object writes and cleanup by job/epoch; then run the regression cases above against both local fixtures and production-like storage/broker configuration.",
    "answerSha256": "daa3b17013ad9e19f989764775706a277ad9068f6477ab1593ceb5107a0f835e",
    "returnedSourceRefs": [
      "evidence_qa078_api_storage",
      "evidence_qa078_security"
    ],
    "omittedBytes": 0,
    "unavailableReason": null
  },
